  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25218776",
      "title": "What is NextJS?",
      "lectureOrder": 416,
      "videoOrder": 383,
      "sourceHash": "bf66f0fea4585d1e9e14dbf24dd89164bbe0ece04d3ff2a64d3b5e36d4e2cdce",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.4,
          "end": 5.88,
          "en": "So, what is NextJS?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.88,
          "end": 10.47,
          "en": "And why could learning NextJS be a good idea?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.47,
          "end": 13.27,
          "en": "And why could NextJS in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.27,
          "end": 17.13,
          "en": "be helpful to us as a React developer?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.13,
          "end": 22.11,
          "en": "If we visit nextjs.org, the official NextJS website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 22.11,
          "end": 27.11,
          "en": "we learn that NextJS is the react framework for production.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 28.13,
          "end": 30.25,
          "en": "Okay, so that sounds like a good argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 30.25,
          "end": 32.49,
          "en": "We all want to build production apps, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.49,
          "end": 37.09,
          "en": "So NextJS is certainly helpful then, but wait a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 37.09,
          "end": 39.54,
          "en": "What exactly does this mean?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 39.54,
          "end": 44.47,
          "en": "So NextJS calls itself a React framework for production",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 44.47,
          "end": 46.11,
          "en": "and that name makes a lot of sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.11,
          "end": 50.49,
          "en": "because NextJS offers a lot of features that make building",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 50.49,
          "end": 54.93,
          "en": "large scale production ready, React apps easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 54.93,
          "end": 58.13,
          "en": "But I personally also like to call NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 59.02,
          "end": 62.71,
          "en": "a full stack framework for ReactJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 62.71,
          "end": 64.57,
          "en": "And it's the full stack part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 64.57,
          "end": 66.2,
          "en": "which I want to highlight here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 66.2,
          "end": 67.43,
          "en": "But I will come back to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.43,
          "end": 71.27,
          "en": "Let's first of all, focus on the framework part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 71.27,
          "end": 76.27,
          "en": "Isn't ReactJS itself, already a framework or a library?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.87,
          "end": 78.15,
          "en": "Well, indeed it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.15,
          "end": 80.9,
          "en": "React is labeled a JavaScript library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.9,
          "end": 83.15,
          "en": "for building user interfaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.15,
          "end": 86.03,
          "en": "And that means that it's a third party package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.03,
          "end": 88.93,
          "en": "which you can add to your front end projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.93,
          "end": 92.58,
          "en": "So it's all about client side Java script code in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.58,
          "end": 94.25,
          "en": "And you can use React there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.25,
          "end": 97.02000000000001,
          "en": "to build interactive user interfaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.02000000000001,
          "end": 98.82,
          "en": "And it's a library that makes building",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.82,
          "end": 102.09,
          "en": "complex user interfaces way easier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.09,
          "end": 105.17,
          "en": "than it would be with just JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.17,
          "end": 107.88,
          "en": "I got separate courses and videos on React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.88,
          "end": 110.25999999999999,
          "en": "where I explain why React is awesome.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.25999999999999,
          "end": 112.4,
          "en": "So I'll not focus on this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.4,
          "end": 114.84,
          "en": "So React already is such a library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.84,
          "end": 117.44,
          "en": "and it's called a library because in its core,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.44,
          "end": 121.02,
          "en": "it's really only focusing on that user interface part,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.02,
          "end": 123.68,
          "en": "on components, state props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.68,
          "end": 126.88,
          "en": "If you want to build large scale React projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.88,
          "end": 131.19,
          "en": "you typically also need to add extra libraries for routing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.19,
          "end": 135,
          "en": "maybe libraries that help you with authentication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135,
          "end": 136.72,
          "en": "and things like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.72,
          "end": 139.61,
          "en": "Now NextJS is labeled a framework",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.61,
          "end": 142.57,
          "en": "and a framework that builds up on React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.57,
          "end": 145.14,
          "en": "Now the difference between a framework and a library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.14,
          "end": 148.13,
          "en": "in the end is that a framework is bigger.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.13,
          "end": 150.26,
          "en": "It has more features than a library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.26,
          "end": 154.07999999999998,
          "en": "It's focusing on more things instead of just a single thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.07999999999998,
          "end": 156.85,
          "en": "And it's also giving you clear rules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.85,
          "end": 160.14,
          "en": "a clear guidance on how you should write your code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.14,
          "end": 162.99,
          "en": "how you should structure your files and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.99,
          "end": 166.63,
          "en": "And all these are things which NextJS does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.63,
          "end": 169.3,
          "en": "as you're going to learn from this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.3,
          "end": 170.66,
          "en": "But it's also a framework",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.66,
          "end": 174.02,
          "en": "building up on another library already on React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.02,
          "end": 176.77,
          "en": "because it enhances React, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.77,
          "end": 180.4,
          "en": "It makes building large scale React apps easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.4,
          "end": 182.27,
          "en": "And that's the part where we're back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.27,
          "end": 185.54,
          "en": "on this for production part here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.54,
          "end": 188.9,
          "en": "NextJS has the goal to make the life easier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.9,
          "end": 191.14,
          "en": "for you as a React developer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.14,
          "end": 192.73,
          "en": "And it builds up on React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.73,
          "end": 196.91,
          "en": "it enhances React by adding many core features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.91,
          "end": 201.44,
          "en": "which you have to add to React apps on your own otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 201.44,
          "end": 204.6,
          "en": "Things like routing, but also many other things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 204.6,
          "end": 207.27,
          "en": "And I'll come back to that in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 207.27,
          "end": 210.07999999999998,
          "en": "And we're going to dive into the key features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 210.07999999999998,
          "end": 212.39,
          "en": "added by NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 212.39,
          "end": 217.3,
          "en": "But NextJS simply adds a lot of features to your React app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.3,
          "end": 219.6,
          "en": "They then are there out of the box",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 219.6,
          "end": 222.95,
          "en": "once you start using NextJS and it definitely ensures",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.95,
          "end": 226.67000000000002,
          "en": "that you don't have to reinvent the wheel as often.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.67000000000002,
          "end": 230,
          "en": "You don't have to add as many third party libraries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 230,
          "end": 234.1,
          "en": "to solve common problems, which you need in bigger apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 234.1,
          "end": 236.45,
          "en": "in which you typically need to solve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 236.45,
          "end": 239.81,
          "en": "when building real production React apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 239.81,
          "end": 243,
          "en": "And that's why NextJS is called a framework",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 243,
          "end": 245.72,
          "en": "because it has a lot of features, clear rules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 245.72,
          "end": 247.97,
          "en": "Why it's a framework for React;",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 247.97,
          "end": 249.64,
          "en": "because it builds up on React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 249.64,
          "end": 252.18,
          "en": "It enhances React, it uses React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 252.18,
          "end": 253.97,
          "en": "You still write React code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 253.97,
          "end": 256.37,
          "en": "You still build React components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 256.37,
          "end": 258.41,
          "en": "but it's a framework for production",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 258.41,
          "end": 261.05,
          "en": "because it adds all those missing features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 261.05,
          "end": 264.19,
          "en": "which you typically do need to add to React apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 264.19,
          "end": 266.52,
          "en": "to really prepare them for production",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 266.52,
          "end": 269,
          "en": "and to solve common problems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 269,
          "end": 271.44,
          "en": "And with that, let's now take a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 271.44,
          "end": 274.96,
          "en": "at the actual features added by NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 274.96,
          "end": 278.25,
          "en": "so that we understand where it helps us exactly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 278.25,
          "end": 283.123,
          "en": "and why using it is a great idea and makes our life easier.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
